[i]You approach the clean looking house. Smoke rises from its chimney as a waft of herbs and strangely isopropyl alcohol hits your nose[/i]

[i]You ring the doorbell[/i]

[i]The door swings open to a black robed figure wearing a bird mask. She beckons you inside as she returns to toiling her cauldron, bubbling with strange liquids and smells[/i]

WITCH: “Hello. You are a new patient, am I correct? Luck is on your side then, for I am available for one last checkup. Tell me what you need—and keep it brief. You may be my patient, but I have other matters to attend to”

MC: “Uhm… Trick or treat?”

WITCH: “Interesting. But a patient does not receive a treat until after the appointment, no?”

[i]She fishes for the bonesaw strapped to her belt, and starts to idly polish its blade. Both her goggles and the sharp metal gleam under the dim lighting—her intentions are clear[/i]

